Article 15 Exceptions to Breeder's Rights  
(1) [Compulsory Exceptions] Breeder's rights shall not extend to:  
(i) acts done privately and for non-commercial purposes;  
(ii) acts done for experimental purposes;  
(iii) acts done for the purpose of breeding other varieties, except where the provisions of Article 14(5) apply, and acts referred to in Article 14(1) to (4) in relation to such other varieties.

