Article 7  Division of Application and Registration  

I. [Division of Application]  
(1) Any application (hereinafter referred to as the "original application") involving multiple goods or services may be divided by the applicant or upon the applicant's request into two or more applications (hereinafter referred to as "divisional applications"), each covering goods or services listed in the original application, under the following circumstances:  
(1) at least before the trademark authority makes a decision on the registrability of the trademark;  
(2) during any opposition proceedings against the registration decision made by the trademark authority;  
(3) during any appeal proceedings against the registration decision made by the trademark authority.

7. [Date of Receipt] Each Contracting Party may determine the circumstances in which any document submitted or any fee paid to the following entities or at the following addresses shall be deemed to have been received by its Office: 

(1) a branch or sub-office of the Office; 

(2) where the Contracting Party is an intergovernmental organization referred to in Article 26(1)(ii), an Office which is acting on behalf of that Contracting Party; 

(3) an official postal service; 

(4) a delivery service or agency designated by the Contracting Party; 

(5) an address other than an address designated by the Office.

IV. [Exceptions under Article 14(3) of the Treaty]  
The exceptions provided for in Article 14(3) of the Treaty refer to failure to comply with the following time limits:  

(1) Time limits for which relief has been granted under Article 14(2) of the Treaty;  
(2) Time limits for submitting a request for relief under Article 14 of the Treaty;  
(3) Time limits for the payment of renewal fees;  
(4) Time limits for taking action before an appeal board or other review body within the Office;  
(5) Time limits for taking action in inter partes proceedings;  
(6) Time limits for submitting the declarations referred to in Article 3(1)(a)(vii) or Article 3(1)(a)(viii) of the Treaty;  
(7) Time limits for submitting a declaration, under the law of the Contracting Party, that may result in the assignment of a new filing date to a pending application;  
(8) Time limits for amending or adding a priority claim.
